AB  - Deceptive news has an intention to defame a person, an institution or an organization. It often has a catastrophic effect on the views of the readers. With the advancement of technology, social media and online sites are made so accessible that, it acts as a catalyst for spreading fake news. Identification of such misinformation is a challenging task even for humans. But with Deep learning and Machine learning techniques, there have been efforts to solve this problem. In this paper the influence of linguistic characteristics and contextual features in fake news detection are analyzed and certain techniques like Naive Bayes, KNN, SVM, Decision tree, Hybrid CNN, CMS etc. are compared.
