AB  - In the age of the Internet, access to information is no longer a concern, the credibility, however, is the new era challenge. Information reaches people in an unfiltered format and therefore raises questions about the authenticity, validity, and credibility. This paper focuses on increasing the reliability of the news, concentrating on static analysis of written text intending to detect possible disingenuous information. To achieve this goal, intelligent solutions were engaged, designed to detect patterns of fake articles that can hint at the lack of knowledge or outright maliciously. The architecture, of the proposed fake news detection system is a composite solution of different classification algorithms, with a final network output obtained through the use of the ensemble learning methods, respectively the comparison of three voting systems. The baseline model allowed a satisfactory accuracy of 99% for the given dataset.
