AU  - Aleroud, A
AU  - Yang, YF
AU  - Melhem, A
AU  - Rutland, J
T2  - SOCIAL MEDIA + SOCIETY
AB  - The purpose of this article is to explore Arabic-language Tweets based out of Saudi Arabia to investigate the social media landscape. Specifically, this article seeks to address the question, "What thematic issues concerning the U.S. socio-political landscape are present in Arabic-language Twitter postings?" And, "To what extent can these issues be described as propagandic in nature?" To do so, we propose a machine-learning and artificial intelligence span detection approach to identify propaganda Tweets in Middle Eastern Countries, with a focus on Saudi Arabia. As opposed to previous work, this article maps and investigates different propaganda categories using the BEND Social Cyber Security framework. This article then proceeds to a case study analysis of state-sponsored targeted propaganda from Saudi Arabia and briefly describes the categories of propaganda uncovered. We then relate those categories to the BEND Framework and conclude with policy recommendations and discussion.
