TI  - Applying Evidential Pluralism to Justify Legal Responses to Online Fake News
AU  - Trofimov, A
T2  - PHILOSOPHY OF THE SOCIAL SCIENCES
AB  - The aim of this paper is to argue that Evidential Pluralism ought to be used to evaluate the impact of online fake news. To support this, I show how an application of Evidential Pluralism can overcome difficulties in assessing the impact of online fake news. The significance of this is twofold. Firstly, the application of Evidential Pluralism enables an evidence-based justification for legal interventions aimed at tackling online fake news. Secondly, the application of Evidential Pluralism to the problem of online fake news provides a case study example to motivate a new methodology for evidence-based law, called EBL+.
