AB  - The use of Generative Adversarial Networks is almost traditional in creating synthetic images for medical purposes. They are probably the best use of GANs until now, as their results can easily be checked by the eye of specialists. In fake news detection models, we have seen lately that neural models (and deep learning) can provide a considerable improvement from standard classifiers. Yet, the most problematic problem still is the lack of data, mostly fake news data to feed these models. In this paper, we address that by proposing the use of a GAN. Results show a better capacity to generalize when used for training an extended dataset based on synthetic samples created by this GAN.
